  "findings": [
    "Existing mango sources already provide many small-object boxes, but the inspected canopy samples are predominantly dark/artificially lit. MangoFruitBD adds daylight variety; many images remain closeups and some are off-tree.",
    "Dragon orchard frames add small fruit amid branches; they are seven recording groups, not 2448 independent scenes. Some visible partial/distant fruit are unlabeled in inspected source images.",
    "MangoFruitBD contains two exact duplicate image pairs, one crossing its original train/validation folders. Project preparation removes exact duplicates before making new splits.",
    "Pose/disease labels supervise species detection only. New orchard imports are never used as ripeness labels.",
    "Source ZIP CRC and image decoding checked during import. Whole-archive SHA256 values are publisher metadata, not verified whole-file checksums.",
    "Old Roboflow polygon labels previously parsed as boxes are now converted correctly. Old detector/dragon-classifier checkpoints require retraining.",
    "Target-orchard accuracy and exhaustive annotation quality remain unproven. Keep an independent field test. RF Fresh/Defect source names still require maturity-label review.",
    "Inspected dragon orchard frames predominantly show red fruit; broad unripe-on-plant coverage has not been established.",
    "Dragon recording allocation uses frame counts; the corrected split avoids putting only the 23-frame clip in validation."
  ],
